            {
                "Turning eighteen marks the transition from childhood into adulthood—a stage that brings both freedom and responsibility. As I enter this new chapter of my life, I often find myself wandering through the darkest corners of my thoughts, filled with doubts and uncertainty. It feels as though I keep untying the same knots only to end up back where I started. I do not always know which path to take or where the \"right\" destination truly is, and that uncertainty often leaves me questioning myself.",
                "Learning St. Augustine’s life helped me realize that life is a journey of constant searching, learning, and returning to God. His story showed me that people make mistakes, struggle with temptations, and sometimes lose their way, yet God's mercy remains present. Romans 12:2 reminds me not to conform to the ways of the world but to remain firm in my faith, allowing God to transform my mind and heart. St. Augustine's life also reminded me of my own younger years—times when I resisted my parents, wanted things my own way, and slowly stepped out of my comfort zone to discover who I am. Like him, I am still learning to understand my actions, emotions, and thoughts as I continue to grow.",
