                "Lord, you know me better than I know myself. For a long time, I have struggled with a kind of noise inside my own head. I don't always understand why I act the way I do, or feel the way I feel. I have asked myself, again and again, why I exist the way I do, and most of the time I don't get an answer. This questioning has worn me down. It felt like a constant, quiet pain that never really went away, no matter how much I tried to think my way out of it. I didn't realize back then that I was looking for answers in the wrong place, inside myself, when I should have been looking toward you.",
